# Spike S3 local ignores — generated output + Rust build artifacts.
#
# Generated result files (report.json / summary.md) are intentionally NOT
# committed: they are host/time-specific evidence, never source of truth.
# `Cargo.lock` IS committed (reproducible standalone build). This spike never
# executes Nix, never reaches the network, never mutates `/nix`, and never
# signs/notarizes. Detect mode DOES run the read-only
# `/usr/bin/security find-identity` probe, so a live Detect reads identity
# metadata/counts from the default keychain (never credentials, never writes
# keychain data); unit/Fake tests never access the keychain.

/out/
/report.json
/summary.md

# Rust build artifacts (mirrors the repo-root .gitignore intent for `target`).
/target/
**/target/
